1
00:01:14,875 --> 00:01:18,083
Mind the lasers, Lord Duke.
You may trigger the alarm.

2
00:01:18,166 --> 00:01:19,833
Please go through the--

3
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:26,875
How did you get in here?

4
00:01:26,958 --> 00:01:29,791
How did you bypass my security system?

5
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:32,166
As you can see, it wasn't that secure.

6
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:36,166
Still, I assure you it'll be much easier
to steal <i>Lady with an Ermine.</i>

7
00:01:36,250 --> 00:01:37,583
Will it?

8
00:01:37,666 --> 00:01:38,875
Aim for his head.

9
00:01:52,666 --> 00:01:53,916
What are they doing here?

10
00:01:56,125 --> 00:01:57,291
Waiting for you.

11
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:08,500
We could have left as easily as we came in

12
00:02:08,583 --> 00:02:13,166
and be already 500 km away
with your Modigliani and your Rembrandt.

13
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:15,875
I'd estimate this collection is worth

14
00:02:15,958 --> 00:02:17,916
over a billion euros.

15
00:02:20,458 --> 00:02:22,833
<i>Then why phone me instead of leaving?</i>

16
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:27,625
Because there's something
I need you to understand.

17
00:02:28,208 --> 00:02:31,958
In this business,
there's a fundamental element, trust.

18
00:02:34,458 --> 00:02:38,166
Now you know that I'll do that job
and that I'm an honorable partner.

19
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:49,166
And you know my loyalty is above

20
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:51,958
the billion euros
I could have stolen from you.

21
00:03:14,208 --> 00:03:16,083
Answer it, please.

22
00:03:16,166 --> 00:03:17,708
This is your home.

23
00:03:24,291 --> 00:03:25,791
- Hello.
<i>- It's Santos, sir.</i>

24
00:03:25,875 --> 00:03:27,625
Some men want to rob you.

25
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:30,916
<i>They shot me, kidnapped me,</i>
<i>and stole my truck, the bastards.</i>

26
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
They have all the keys to your estate.

27
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:34,750
I know, Santos. I know.

28
00:03:34,833 --> 00:03:37,208
I know them.
Everything's in order, all right?

29
00:03:37,291 --> 00:03:41,416
From now on, these gentlemen
are welcome in my estate.

30
00:03:48,625 --> 00:03:49,875
For fuck's sake.

31
00:03:49,958 --> 00:03:51,958
Goddammit.

32
00:03:58,375 --> 00:03:59,666
Hey! Kid?

33
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:02,333
You see, there was a misunderstanding.

34
00:04:02,416 --> 00:04:03,791
Come, I'll help you up.

35
00:04:07,416 --> 00:04:10,125
Get away from him.
Hands on your fucking head.

36
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:14,125
Go inside.

37
00:04:27,916 --> 00:04:30,583
I'm impressed

38
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:34,083
by the lengths you went to
to earn my trust, and,

39
00:04:34,583 --> 00:04:35,750
honestly,

40
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:38,250
you have.

41
00:04:39,833 --> 00:04:42,333
- Sherry?
- Please.

42
00:04:42,416 --> 00:04:43,583
Sherry.

43
00:04:43,666 --> 00:04:48,416
Now that we're beginning
to enjoy this friendship, Lord Duke,

44
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,541
may I ask something?

45
00:04:50,750 --> 00:04:51,958
Of course.

46
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:56,208
What do you do here,
with this magnificent collection,

47
00:04:56,708 --> 00:04:59,458
in this cozy room, with a bed…?

48
00:05:01,625 --> 00:05:04,916
I spend more nights than you'd think here.

49
00:05:05,416 --> 00:05:07,125
This is

50
00:05:07,208 --> 00:05:08,291
my secret place.

51
00:05:08,791 --> 00:05:10,916
Well, not anymore.

52
00:05:12,958 --> 00:05:15,083
It's exclusively dedicated

53
00:05:16,333 --> 00:05:17,541
to beauty.

54
00:05:18,875 --> 00:05:20,500
Do you know what beauty is?

55
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:22,750
I have a vague idea.

56
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:26,166
To me, it's waking up in that bed,

57
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:29,458
with my wife,

58
00:05:31,125 --> 00:05:32,500
and allowing

59
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,208
the light of dawn

60
00:05:35,875 --> 00:05:38,916
to come in through that skylight
and illuminate…

61
00:05:40,250 --> 00:05:42,208
Vermeer's <i>The Concert.</i>

62
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,416
It thrills me to think

63
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:47,833
I'm the only person

64
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:50,375
on the face of the Earth

65
00:05:50,458 --> 00:05:53,000
who can feel

66
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:56,708
the joy of contemplating it.

67
00:05:57,500 --> 00:06:03,583
To know that this collection
is just for me.

68
00:06:04,625 --> 00:06:06,250
As if Raphael,

69
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:11,666
Monet, or Caravaggio

70
00:06:13,541 --> 00:06:16,791
had painted… for me.

71
00:06:18,208 --> 00:06:20,333
When people have a lot of money,

72
00:06:20,416 --> 00:06:22,291
they spend it on what pleases them.

73
00:06:22,375 --> 00:06:26,875
They buy houses, yachts, bunkers.

74
00:06:26,958 --> 00:06:28,625
I have my golden sand,

75
00:06:28,708 --> 00:06:32,833
the aroma of my wine casks, my bulls,

76
00:06:32,916 --> 00:06:34,166
and I have…

77
00:06:48,041 --> 00:06:49,541
my collection.

78
00:06:52,291 --> 00:06:56,625
Is this a satisfactory explanation?
Come with me.

79
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:59,750
Fuck me. Why won't you listen, dammit?

80
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:01,166
I'll be damned.

81
00:07:02,541 --> 00:07:05,583
You're late to the party.
Don't you see I was helping him?

82
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:08,958
Think I'll believe you?
After you almost bit my face off?

83
00:07:09,041 --> 00:07:12,666
But that's over now.
My boss is at the estate with yours.

84
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:15,083
I just talked to him on the phone.

85
00:07:17,375 --> 00:07:20,000
How? There's no signal at the estate.

86
00:07:20,083 --> 00:07:24,333
Of course not. It's full of jammers.
I called the landline.

87
00:07:25,208 --> 00:07:28,500
Don't move,
or I'll blow your fucking head off.

88
00:07:30,083 --> 00:07:32,250
I just wanted to grab the cell phone

89
00:07:32,833 --> 00:07:34,458
so you can see I'm not lying.

90
00:07:37,666 --> 00:07:38,791
Let me see you.

91
00:07:47,708 --> 00:07:49,541
What's your boss called?

92
00:07:49,625 --> 00:07:50,875
Yeah.

93
00:07:50,958 --> 00:07:52,416
Go to "recent calls."

94
00:07:59,291 --> 00:08:00,833
We can start negotiating.

95
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,875
Do answer. I'm sure it's not for us.

96
00:08:13,125 --> 00:08:14,583
- Hello?
<i>- Good evening.</i>

97
00:08:14,666 --> 00:08:16,041
Is Berlin there?

98
00:08:17,708 --> 00:08:18,708
Oh, well.

99
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,333
It is for you.

100
00:08:25,708 --> 00:08:27,958
- Who's this?
<i>- It's Roi, sir.</i>

101
00:08:28,041 --> 00:08:30,041
The guard says we're with the duke now.

102
00:08:30,125 --> 00:08:31,416
<i>Is that true?</i>

103
00:08:33,708 --> 00:08:34,875
That's right.

104
00:08:34,958 --> 00:08:36,458
What do we do with this guy?

105
00:08:36,541 --> 00:08:38,791
<i>Nothing, Roi. Everything's all right.</i>

106
00:08:39,875 --> 00:08:41,375
We just let him go?

107
00:08:41,458 --> 00:08:44,625
That man must need rest or a doctor.

108
00:08:44,708 --> 00:08:47,291
He's had enough excitement for tonight.

109
00:08:58,583 --> 00:09:01,833
I told you. We're together now.

110
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:04,583
On the same side.

111
00:09:07,791 --> 00:09:08,625
Not yet.

112
00:09:10,708 --> 00:09:12,666
That's for my time in the river.

113
00:09:13,166 --> 00:09:14,750
We're even for now.

114
00:09:17,791 --> 00:09:20,166
Now we can discuss important matters.

115
00:09:21,291 --> 00:09:24,166
How much will you charge
for stealing <i>Lady with an Ermine?</i>

116
00:09:25,041 --> 00:09:27,291
How about 35 million?

117
00:09:28,916 --> 00:09:30,041
It's not stealing it.

118
00:09:30,125 --> 00:09:33,375
It's planning the heist,
risking our freedom to execute it,

119
00:09:33,458 --> 00:09:34,625
guarding the painting

120
00:09:34,708 --> 00:09:40,125
until we confirm the police have no leads,
and finally, handing it to you, safely,

121
00:09:40,208 --> 00:09:42,000
for your personal enjoyment.

122
00:09:42,083 --> 00:09:45,958
If we bear in mind that the ten
best paid art pieces in history

123
00:09:46,041 --> 00:09:47,833
add up to more than $200 million,

124
00:09:47,916 --> 00:09:51,416
and that Da Vinci is, undoubtedly,
the master of all masters,

125
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,875
I'd say 35 million is even a steal.

126
00:09:56,083 --> 00:09:57,291
Please.

127
00:09:58,083 --> 00:09:59,250
Don't justify yourself.

128
00:10:00,208 --> 00:10:01,625
Did you see me blink?

129
00:10:02,125 --> 00:10:03,500
No, did you?

130
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:08,625
That means the figure seems correct to me.

131
00:10:11,583 --> 00:10:14,750
I'll also need
four or five million in advance,

132
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:16,125
in 40,000-euro bundles

133
00:10:16,208 --> 00:10:19,208
of unmarked, nonsequential,
used 100-euro bills.

134
00:10:19,291 --> 00:10:21,958
When you have the money, call me.

135
00:10:22,541 --> 00:10:24,416
I already have that money.

136
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:29,416
Come to my house
for breakfast tomorrow at 10:00 a.m.

137
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,916
Is that agreeable?

138
00:11:08,583 --> 00:11:10,958
Where will he get
all that money in five hours?

139
00:11:11,791 --> 00:11:13,625
That's not the right question, Roi.

140
00:11:13,708 --> 00:11:14,833
I can answer that.

141
00:11:14,916 --> 00:11:17,041
Those four or five million euros

142
00:11:17,125 --> 00:11:20,583
in nonsequential unmarked bills
won't come from an ATM.

143
00:11:24,166 --> 00:11:27,000
Or from a bank's safe
because today's Sunday.

144
00:11:37,083 --> 00:11:40,458
Unless the guy
has his own money-making machine,

145
00:11:40,541 --> 00:11:45,666
I'd say he has bundles of money hidden
in some mysterious place.

146
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:49,500
Money of dubious origin. Undeclared money.

147
00:11:50,083 --> 00:11:52,333
No one funds a heist
with their own fortune.

148
00:11:52,416 --> 00:11:57,500
- Now, what's the right question, Roi?
- Where is that dirty money?

149
00:11:58,458 --> 00:11:59,458
Bingo.

150
00:11:59,541 --> 00:12:02,333
That man has a hidden fortune.

151
00:12:02,416 --> 00:12:04,833
He keeps it close. Without paying taxes.

152
00:12:04,916 --> 00:12:08,125
And that's exactly
what we'll steal from that bastard.

153
00:12:08,208 --> 00:12:09,875
It must be a ton of money, right?

154
00:12:09,958 --> 00:12:12,458
His collection has what, 15 paintings?

155
00:12:12,541 --> 00:12:15,500
Say he paid 20 or 30 million for each…

156
00:12:15,583 --> 00:12:18,041
About 300 or 450 million euros.

157
00:12:18,625 --> 00:12:22,250
And where does a Spanish nobleman
such as our duke

158
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:26,041
get 300 or 450 undeclared millions?

159
00:12:26,541 --> 00:12:28,416
Not from the wineries.

160
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,041
Or from his cattle business.

161
00:12:30,125 --> 00:12:31,125
From the yachts.

162
00:12:34,416 --> 00:12:37,083
Ferrying celebrities back and forth
can't make much.

163
00:12:37,166 --> 00:12:39,666
It can, if you also move something else.

164
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:41,916
We should look into that, right?

165
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,625
Why would we want to know
where he gets his money?

166
00:12:44,708 --> 00:12:45,833
I am interested.

167
00:12:46,416 --> 00:12:50,291
The more we know about him,
the more we'll have him by the balls.

168
00:12:50,791 --> 00:12:53,666
I'll go.
I can go undercover in one of the yachts.

169
00:12:54,583 --> 00:12:55,583
By myself.

170
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,500
Great.

171
00:13:00,250 --> 00:13:04,125
I'm sorry your reconciliation with Roi
couldn't be,

172
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:07,708
because I suspect what you want
is not to investigate, but to get away.

173
00:13:08,208 --> 00:13:09,833
Away from him.

174
00:13:10,708 --> 00:13:11,666
Yes.

175
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:12,875
Then so be it.

176
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:16,041
No, it's too risky.
She's not going undercover by herself.

177
00:13:16,125 --> 00:13:17,500
If she wants to go, she'll go.

178
00:13:18,375 --> 00:13:20,375
She'll have to grow up sometime.

179
00:13:20,458 --> 00:13:23,208
But since I'm the leader of the crew,

180
00:13:23,291 --> 00:13:26,791
I have the right to know what Roi did
that's so atrocious

181
00:13:26,875 --> 00:13:30,083
you can't even be on the same boat as him.

182
00:13:44,541 --> 00:13:46,250
He pushed me into the void.

183
00:13:51,833 --> 00:13:53,166
You answer, please.

184
00:13:55,666 --> 00:13:56,750
Hello?

185
00:13:57,583 --> 00:13:58,583
<i>Hi, kitten.</i>

186
00:14:01,916 --> 00:14:03,708
Her ex-boyfriend showed up one day.

187
00:14:03,791 --> 00:14:05,958
And that got your blood boiling?

188
00:14:06,041 --> 00:14:08,750
It wasn't me that visit threw off kilter.

189
00:14:08,833 --> 00:14:10,333
<i>Nora told me you lived here.</i>

190
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:13,250
<i>I told her I was coming to play here</i>
<i>and… coincidence.</i>

191
00:14:14,125 --> 00:14:15,166
<i>Hey.</i>

192
00:14:15,750 --> 00:14:16,958
<i>Why don't you come down?</i>

193
00:14:21,250 --> 00:14:22,666
I can't.

194
00:14:23,416 --> 00:14:26,208
- Who is it?
<i>- Come on down so we can chat for a bit.</i>

195
00:14:29,708 --> 00:14:32,000
I said I'm not going down. Go away.

196
00:14:32,083 --> 00:14:34,583
<i>Our life was a fucking fire, sure.</i>

197
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:36,875
<i>We should be able</i>
<i>to discuss it face to face.</i>

198
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:41,708
At that moment,
I should have realized she's sick.

199
00:14:43,166 --> 00:14:44,250
Shut up.

200
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:46,166
But I didn't see it.

201
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:47,750
I didn't want to.

202
00:14:47,833 --> 00:14:49,166
You screwed up my life.

203
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:50,583
Calm down. It's okay.

204
00:14:50,666 --> 00:14:53,583
I won't calm down, dammit!
Not until that guy goes away!

205
00:14:53,666 --> 00:14:55,291
I only wanted to help her.

206
00:14:57,875 --> 00:14:59,666
Dude, she doesn't want to go down.

207
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:00,875
Let it be.

208
00:15:00,958 --> 00:15:03,458
<i>I'm not leaving</i>
<i>until she comes down, okay?</i>

209
00:15:06,333 --> 00:15:07,708
Help you stop that pain.

210
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:12,791
Or that rancor, whatever.

211
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:17,708
Go the fuck away!

212
00:15:19,458 --> 00:15:21,208
Roi, I asked you for help.

213
00:15:21,791 --> 00:15:24,666
Come down! I just want to talk, you hear?

214
00:15:25,458 --> 00:15:27,333
- Calm down, okay?
- I want him to go!

215
00:15:27,416 --> 00:15:29,166
Come down, please!

216
00:15:31,083 --> 00:15:32,291
Breathe.

217
00:15:32,375 --> 00:15:34,125
I'm breathing, Roi, okay?

218
00:15:34,208 --> 00:15:37,875
I won't leave until we wrap up our story,
you hear me?

219
00:15:39,583 --> 00:15:41,208
Someone has to go down.

220
00:15:41,291 --> 00:15:42,875
Or he won't leave.

221
00:15:43,541 --> 00:15:45,416
Go down and rough him up.

222
00:15:48,291 --> 00:15:49,375
I can't.

223
00:15:49,875 --> 00:15:50,875
Why not?

224
00:15:52,083 --> 00:15:53,583
Because it has to be you.

225
00:15:55,416 --> 00:15:57,375
You go and face him.

226
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,833
You can do it.

227
00:16:01,833 --> 00:16:04,166
You're no longer the girl
who fell for him.

228
00:16:05,916 --> 00:16:06,916
You are firm now.

229
00:16:08,541 --> 00:16:10,083
You are brave, dammit.

230
00:16:13,333 --> 00:16:14,333
Look.

231
00:16:16,375 --> 00:16:19,583
You go and tell him it's over.

232
00:16:22,208 --> 00:16:24,000
And close that wound forever.

233
00:16:45,666 --> 00:16:46,875
But that wasn't it.

234
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,916
You didn't want me to close any wounds.

235
00:16:50,791 --> 00:16:54,125
You wanted to look out the balcony
and see how I chose you.

236
00:16:54,208 --> 00:16:55,375
You.

237
00:16:56,333 --> 00:16:59,125
You sent me down
not to overcome my fears, but yours.

238
00:16:59,208 --> 00:17:01,583
Because, deep down, you never trusted me.

239
00:17:01,666 --> 00:17:02,666
Cameron.

240
00:17:03,541 --> 00:17:05,666
I asked you to go down to end a story.

241
00:17:06,416 --> 00:17:07,666
Not to fuck your ex.

242
00:17:52,083 --> 00:17:53,666
This is all your fault.

243
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:55,416
You forced me.

244
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,666
You sent me to him,
knowing I wasn't capable.

245
00:18:01,041 --> 00:18:02,583
You're a pyromaniac.

246
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,250
No self-control.

247
00:18:07,250 --> 00:18:10,125
So unstable
you're incapable of keeping anything.

248
00:18:11,291 --> 00:18:14,041
Every shitty thing that happens to you,
you deserve.

249
00:18:15,958 --> 00:18:17,916
You destroy everything.

250
00:18:19,583 --> 00:18:21,500
You don't care who you hurt.

251
00:18:24,416 --> 00:18:26,583
I'm giving Jimmy a second chance.

252
00:18:28,083 --> 00:18:31,625
Because giving you a chance
only served to remind me of him.

253
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:35,916
I don't wanna see you again.

254
00:18:36,791 --> 00:18:39,000
Delete my number and don't look for me.

255
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,666
If you ever see me in danger,
run the other way.

256
00:20:53,041 --> 00:20:54,458
Good morning, Captain.

257
00:20:58,291 --> 00:20:59,958
We have a date.

258
00:21:01,333 --> 00:21:02,416
Oh, do we?

259
00:21:03,041 --> 00:21:04,500
I didn't remember.

260
00:21:04,583 --> 00:21:07,625
Because you didn't know. But I do.

261
00:21:09,791 --> 00:21:12,083
A treat to thank you
for what you've managed.

262
00:21:12,708 --> 00:21:15,125
For risking our lives driving perilously?

263
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:17,791
And saving you from the police?

264
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:21,916
For something much better and nicer.

265
00:21:22,416 --> 00:21:25,750
For 24 full hours,

266
00:21:26,250 --> 00:21:27,666
I haven't thought of my ex.

267
00:21:28,916 --> 00:21:30,125
Isn't that incredible?

268
00:21:30,625 --> 00:21:31,791
It is to me.

269
00:21:33,666 --> 00:21:36,291
Come on, take a shower.
I left it all ready for you.

270
00:21:36,375 --> 00:21:39,666
And I got these clothes out
for you to wear.

271
00:21:39,750 --> 00:21:42,375
Try them on.
I don't want you to look out of place.

272
00:21:43,250 --> 00:21:45,416
Out of place where?

273
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,291
That's a surprise.

274
00:21:48,666 --> 00:21:50,083
How did you know I lived here?

275
00:21:50,166 --> 00:21:53,125
I found a mooring invoice
for the boat in your wallet,

276
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:55,958
and the thought came to me,

277
00:21:56,041 --> 00:21:59,375
"Can he be one of those men
who come to Seville by boat?"

278
00:21:59,875 --> 00:22:01,208
It turns out you were.

279
00:22:08,708 --> 00:22:11,250
- Good morning, miss.
- We woke him up.

280
00:22:11,333 --> 00:22:13,875
Simón, may we talk for a moment?

281
00:22:15,125 --> 00:22:16,291
- Excuse me.
- Course.

282
00:22:16,375 --> 00:22:17,541
One second.

283
00:22:22,708 --> 00:22:25,500
Damián, I'm taking the day off.

284
00:22:26,083 --> 00:22:27,333
A day off?

285
00:22:27,416 --> 00:22:29,416
You're meeting the duke, remember?

286
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:31,250
To get that thing you asked for.

287
00:22:31,333 --> 00:22:33,708
Four or five million euros
in bundles of 40,000.

288
00:22:33,791 --> 00:22:36,125
I know!

289
00:22:36,208 --> 00:22:39,291
Keila and I worked out the details
for the Ali Baba plan.

290
00:22:39,375 --> 00:22:40,375
Sheer insanity.

291
00:22:40,458 --> 00:22:43,541
I had just gone to bed when she came in.

292
00:22:43,625 --> 00:22:45,375
What the hell's the Ali Baba plan?

293
00:22:45,458 --> 00:22:47,875
An ingenious ploy
that'll lead us to the treasure

294
00:22:47,958 --> 00:22:49,791
when the duke hands you the money.

295
00:22:49,875 --> 00:22:52,041
- Me?
- Damián, I beg you, please.

296
00:22:52,625 --> 00:22:54,500
The hard part is the plan.

297
00:22:54,583 --> 00:22:56,791
That's ready. You'll execute it.

298
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:57,958
Talk to Keila.

299
00:22:58,041 --> 00:23:01,375
And please,
don't forget to take an elegant bag.

300
00:23:01,458 --> 00:23:04,166
I can't stand thieves
who carry bills in metal cases

301
00:23:04,250 --> 00:23:05,625
as if they were drills.

302
00:23:08,291 --> 00:23:09,416
What will you do?

303
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:11,541
Embrace life, brother.

304
00:23:27,625 --> 00:23:32,041
And here's the narrowest street
in Seville.

305
00:23:32,541 --> 00:23:33,791
Know what they call it?

306
00:23:34,875 --> 00:23:36,000
Kiss alley.

307
00:23:43,541 --> 00:23:44,916
And…

308
00:23:45,416 --> 00:23:48,041
Do you know why I brought you here?

309
00:23:50,375 --> 00:23:52,958
I haven't the faintest idea.
I'm on tenterhooks.

310
00:23:53,041 --> 00:23:54,333
Let me tell you.

311
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:57,125
The people
who annoy me the most in the world

312
00:23:57,208 --> 00:23:59,833
are those who save the kiss
for the end of a date.

313
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:01,541
You don't say.

314
00:24:01,625 --> 00:24:03,000
They annoy me so…

315
00:24:04,750 --> 00:24:05,750
Why?

316
00:24:05,833 --> 00:24:09,291
Because they are people
who live life in fear,

317
00:24:09,375 --> 00:24:12,208
who can't live life to the hilt.

318
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:16,375
If they have a smidgen of happiness,
they save it for the end.

319
00:24:17,041 --> 00:24:17,958
Just in case.

320
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:20,291
Just in case what?

321
00:24:20,375 --> 00:24:22,333
In case it gets used up, I don't know.

322
00:24:23,125 --> 00:24:25,625
So they kiss at the end

323
00:24:25,708 --> 00:24:28,125
and go home
with that taste in their mouths.

324
00:24:29,750 --> 00:24:32,166
But I don't think happiness gets used up.

325
00:24:33,125 --> 00:24:35,250
And I, when I really like someone,

326
00:24:36,125 --> 00:24:37,250
I kiss them right away.

327
00:24:45,875 --> 00:24:47,333
And from there, upwards,

328
00:24:47,833 --> 00:24:48,958
like a rocket.

329
00:24:55,416 --> 00:24:57,500
I've wanted to kiss you

330
00:24:57,583 --> 00:25:00,041
since I saw you
flinging things out the window.

331
00:25:02,375 --> 00:25:05,208
And when I went into your house at night.

332
00:25:05,291 --> 00:25:07,500
But it would've been
a bit in bad taste then.

333
00:25:10,833 --> 00:25:12,250
If you'll excuse me, please.

334
00:25:14,791 --> 00:25:17,250
- Step aside.
- Aren't there other streets in Seville?

335
00:25:18,458 --> 00:25:20,083
My God. Walk through.

336
00:25:20,750 --> 00:25:22,666
- There.
- Go.

337
00:25:22,750 --> 00:25:23,916
- There you go.
- Oh.

338
00:25:25,458 --> 00:25:27,166
- This one's a voyeur.
- For sure.

339
00:25:27,250 --> 00:25:29,041
The dog's his cover.

340
00:25:29,125 --> 00:25:31,041
See him looking
from the corner of his eye.

341
00:25:32,791 --> 00:25:33,791
Follow me.

342
00:25:36,666 --> 00:25:37,916
Oh…

343
00:25:39,583 --> 00:25:41,125
Yes, come in.

344
00:25:45,125 --> 00:25:48,083
Could you explain the Ali Baba plan to me?

345
00:25:50,583 --> 00:25:53,125
<i>Know the story</i>
<i>of Ali Baba and the Forty Thieves?</i>

346
00:25:53,208 --> 00:25:54,416
<i>Can't recall much of it.</i>

347
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:57,000
A man discovers where a band of 40 thieves

348
00:25:57,083 --> 00:25:58,750
keep their treasure.

349
00:25:58,833 --> 00:26:00,666
<i>- Okay.</i>
<i>- Hidden in a cave.</i>

350
00:26:00,750 --> 00:26:04,083
It opens if you stand
in front and say, "Open, Sesame."

351
00:26:04,166 --> 00:26:05,500
Yeah, right.

352
00:26:05,583 --> 00:26:06,958
With me.

353
00:26:10,541 --> 00:26:12,333
- You really don't remember?
- Focus.

354
00:26:12,416 --> 00:26:14,500
What's this fucking Ali Baba plan?

355
00:26:14,583 --> 00:26:16,791
To see where the thieves
keep their treasure.

356
00:26:18,541 --> 00:26:21,041
<i>Only in this case, we're not the thieves.</i>

357
00:26:21,833 --> 00:26:23,208
We're Ali Baba.

358
00:26:30,375 --> 00:26:31,791
Ten sharp.

359
00:26:34,083 --> 00:26:37,041
- Why isn't your boss here?
- He's working on the plan.

360
00:26:37,125 --> 00:26:39,916
I'm his right-hand man
and handle the financial side.

361
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:42,833
And the details.
I see you brought your own bag.

362
00:26:42,916 --> 00:26:45,041
Yes, I can't stand those thieves

363
00:26:45,125 --> 00:26:48,041
who carry bills in metal briefcases
as if they were drills.

364
00:26:48,625 --> 00:26:50,000
I completely agree.

365
00:26:51,458 --> 00:26:52,500
Good morning.

366
00:26:53,416 --> 00:26:55,416
Darling, the car is at the door.

367
00:26:55,500 --> 00:26:58,416
Looking at you,
I'm tempted to be irresponsible,

368
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:00,791
but I made these gentlemen get up early.

369
00:27:00,875 --> 00:27:02,250
What will they think of me?

370
00:27:02,333 --> 00:27:04,041
I must attend to them.

371
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:09,458
He's with another woman
and thinks I don't know.

372
00:27:10,791 --> 00:27:13,708
It's so tiresome to compete
with those perfect ladies…

373
00:27:15,875 --> 00:27:17,291
This one has an ermine.

374
00:27:17,375 --> 00:27:19,791
Samuel, please, escort her.

375
00:27:21,166 --> 00:27:24,250
Gentlemen, I'm off with my babysitter.

376
00:27:30,625 --> 00:27:31,625
Anyway…

377
00:27:31,708 --> 00:27:32,833
Shall we start?

378
00:27:32,916 --> 00:27:34,083
Yes.

379
00:27:36,708 --> 00:27:39,208
Here's the money.
I imagine you want to count it.

380
00:27:39,291 --> 00:27:41,500
Yes, my job is to be cautious.

381
00:27:41,583 --> 00:27:45,250
I have friends
who were paid with photocopies.

382
00:27:46,625 --> 00:27:50,625
It's important you take the bag
you'll use to carry the money.

383
00:27:50,708 --> 00:27:51,708
Why?

384
00:27:51,791 --> 00:27:53,875
Because this bundle will be inside.

385
00:28:01,375 --> 00:28:02,583
The first 40,000.

386
00:28:03,083 --> 00:28:04,250
See anything odd?

387
00:28:05,375 --> 00:28:08,750
Unmarked, nonsequential,
used 100-euro bills.

388
00:28:08,833 --> 00:28:09,791
Where's the trick?

389
00:28:09,875 --> 00:28:12,500
The idea is you'll make a big show
of counting it

390
00:28:12,583 --> 00:28:13,916
and putting it in the bag.

391
00:28:15,750 --> 00:28:17,583
3,960,000.

392
00:28:17,666 --> 00:28:19,291
<i>Until at one point…</i>

393
00:28:19,375 --> 00:28:20,625
4,040,000.

394
00:28:20,708 --> 00:28:22,541
Enough. Return that bundle.

395
00:28:22,625 --> 00:28:26,375
And why would I give him
40,000 euros back?

396
00:28:26,458 --> 00:28:28,291
For a good reason.

397
00:28:28,375 --> 00:28:30,708
That will be the moment for the switch.

398
00:28:30,791 --> 00:28:34,000
The switcheroo bundle
has a long-range GPS chip.

399
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:37,583
<i>You must hide it</i>
<i>with the money you return to the duke.</i>

400
00:28:37,666 --> 00:28:40,000
So we'll have the location
of that million.

401
00:28:50,083 --> 00:28:51,541
Anything wrong with my money?

402
00:28:52,125 --> 00:28:53,958
No, nothing at all.

403
00:28:54,458 --> 00:28:57,416
For now, we have enough with four million.

404
00:28:57,500 --> 00:28:58,958
You said five million.

405
00:29:00,041 --> 00:29:02,041
We said four or five.

406
00:29:02,125 --> 00:29:05,166
You bringing five
does you credit as a partner.

407
00:29:06,916 --> 00:29:09,833
And speaks to your generosity and fortune.

408
00:29:11,666 --> 00:29:14,875
Was it a test?
Are you evaluating me as a partner?

409
00:29:15,458 --> 00:29:16,458
Me?

410
00:29:22,875 --> 00:29:25,541
Simón told you
this job is predicated on trust.

411
00:29:27,125 --> 00:29:30,208
- Shall I wrap them in plastic for you?
- No need.

412
00:29:30,291 --> 00:29:31,875
Fine. I'll leave it here.

413
00:29:37,625 --> 00:29:38,625
Come.

414
00:29:40,791 --> 00:29:42,500
Girl, good fish today.

415
00:29:51,208 --> 00:29:52,208
Girl!

416
00:29:54,666 --> 00:29:56,625
Do you have Chinese oranges?

417
00:30:12,666 --> 00:30:13,708
Where are we?

418
00:30:15,208 --> 00:30:16,791
In a secret place.

419
00:30:30,750 --> 00:30:33,250
This is a clandestine party
celebrated every year

420
00:30:33,333 --> 00:30:35,666
for the birthday of two aristocrats.

421
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:38,291
The duchess of Málaga
and the countess of Seville.

422
00:30:45,166 --> 00:30:47,958
Hello. You can't come to the party
on an empty stomach.

423
00:30:49,375 --> 00:30:51,250
People from all classes mingle here.

424
00:30:51,333 --> 00:30:55,166
Aristocrats, bon vivants, artists…

425
00:31:19,375 --> 00:31:21,458
The party lasts 24 hours.

426
00:31:22,833 --> 00:31:25,000
- Shall we?
- Let's.

427
00:32:30,875 --> 00:32:34,666
Samuel, bring me
a glass of godello, please.

428
00:32:44,291 --> 00:32:47,000
I was told it's your birthday.
Happy returns.

429
00:32:47,083 --> 00:32:50,791
I need a word in private.
I'm under constant surveillance.

430
00:32:51,625 --> 00:32:55,458
Third-floor bathroom, the one with
the Niña de los Peines photo on the door.

431
00:32:55,541 --> 00:32:58,333
Wait for me inside in the dark.
And don't lock it.

432
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:24,083
Excuse me, Duchess.

433
00:33:41,583 --> 00:33:43,666
All clear. You may go in.

434
00:33:58,583 --> 00:33:59,541
Duchess…

435
00:34:01,916 --> 00:34:05,375
You ruined my birthday celebration
with my husband last night.

436
00:34:05,458 --> 00:34:07,083
I'm sorry.

437
00:34:07,166 --> 00:34:09,083
Apology not accepted. You owe me one.

438
00:34:09,666 --> 00:34:12,791
I want you to do a job for me.

439
00:34:13,583 --> 00:34:16,083
I want you
to steal my husband's paintings.

440
00:34:16,750 --> 00:34:17,625
All of them.

441
00:34:18,750 --> 00:34:22,208
I'm sure you'll make excellent business
with them in the black market.

442
00:34:22,291 --> 00:34:24,333
Don't think it's that easy.

443
00:34:24,416 --> 00:34:26,875
I'll give you a tip for your troubles.

444
00:34:26,958 --> 00:34:28,583
A million euros in cash.

445
00:34:28,666 --> 00:34:32,416
I don't know if I'm comfortable
with the term "tip."

446
00:34:32,500 --> 00:34:34,791
You'll have it easy. I'll help you get in.

447
00:34:34,875 --> 00:34:37,250
Genoveva, I know the way.

448
00:34:37,750 --> 00:34:39,541
We got in yesterday, without help.

449
00:34:40,375 --> 00:34:41,583
You seem contrarian.

450
00:34:41,666 --> 00:34:44,958
You are overlooking a little detail.

451
00:34:45,791 --> 00:34:46,958
I am a gentleman.

452
00:34:47,041 --> 00:34:50,875
And I gave your husband my word.
Not just me. My partner did too.

453
00:34:52,541 --> 00:34:53,958
I like your partner.

454
00:34:55,458 --> 00:34:56,875
He seems intelligent.

455
00:34:58,333 --> 00:35:02,916
I'm sure he'll realize that my business
proposition is the interesting one.

456
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:06,125
Much more than what Álvaro
asked you to do.

457
00:35:06,208 --> 00:35:10,791
There's undoubtedly
something intriguing in all this.

458
00:35:11,291 --> 00:35:14,125
If I may, can I ask

459
00:35:14,625 --> 00:35:17,000
why you want to betray your husband?

460
00:35:17,500 --> 00:35:19,208
Have you ever been in love?

461
00:35:21,833 --> 00:35:23,958
I wonder if I have ever <i>not </i>been.

462
00:35:26,041 --> 00:35:27,916
When I was 15,

463
00:35:28,416 --> 00:35:31,291
I studied at school
every afternoon from 5:00 to 7:00.

464
00:35:32,333 --> 00:35:36,500
And at 5:30, the boys
from the French school would come over

465
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,291
to ride horses.

466
00:35:38,791 --> 00:35:41,208
We had big stables at my school.

467
00:35:43,791 --> 00:35:47,250
Álvaro was always late
to his riding lessons.

468
00:35:47,333 --> 00:35:48,416
Do you know why?

469
00:35:52,833 --> 00:35:54,666
Instead of going straight to class,

470
00:35:55,958 --> 00:35:58,000
he'd climb a stone wall

471
00:35:59,208 --> 00:36:00,750
to watch me study.

472
00:36:03,916 --> 00:36:05,000
For half an hour…

473
00:36:06,625 --> 00:36:07,666
One hour…

474
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,333
And I never noticed.

475
00:36:12,791 --> 00:36:17,166
Until one day, Sister Inés began to throw
stones at him so he'd get down.

476
00:36:21,875 --> 00:36:23,916
No one's ever looked at me like him.

477
00:36:26,541 --> 00:36:28,875
And he's done it for 20 years.

478
00:36:34,333 --> 00:36:35,458
Until now.

479
00:36:39,041 --> 00:36:41,208
Now his eyes are for his collection.

480
00:36:42,041 --> 00:36:43,583
That's why it must disappear.

481
00:36:44,333 --> 00:36:46,041
What do you expect will happen?

482
00:36:47,208 --> 00:36:48,666
Have you wondered what'll happen

483
00:36:48,750 --> 00:36:51,666
if, even after the art is gone,
he doesn't look at you?

484
00:36:52,958 --> 00:36:54,375
What do you mean?

485
00:36:54,458 --> 00:36:57,750
That maybe your husband started
to feel passion for those works

486
00:36:57,833 --> 00:36:59,750
because he stopped feeling it for you.

487
00:37:01,333 --> 00:37:04,958
Maybe life is not
about killing the lover, you see?

488
00:37:05,958 --> 00:37:10,375
But about making it so they choose us
among so many appetizing people.

489
00:37:12,125 --> 00:37:14,291
What an elegant way to refuse me.

490
00:37:16,708 --> 00:37:18,708
I won't deny that you made me think.

491
00:37:19,500 --> 00:37:22,583
You may even have sparked an idea.

492
00:37:24,583 --> 00:37:28,666
But I hope you know that, in negotiations,
I'm as relentless as my husband.

493
00:37:29,250 --> 00:37:32,750
And you won't leave this party
without accepting my assignment.

494
00:37:34,375 --> 00:37:35,583
Because…

495
00:37:36,833 --> 00:37:39,625
with the police hot on your trail,

496
00:37:39,708 --> 00:37:42,958
I don't think you can steal
<i>Lady with an Ermine.</i>

497
00:37:59,916 --> 00:38:02,666
Keila, we're out of the palace.
Does the tracker work?

498
00:38:02,750 --> 00:38:04,125
Yes. The chip is active,

499
00:38:04,208 --> 00:38:06,625
and the money hasn't moved from the room.

500
00:38:07,208 --> 00:38:09,750
Bruce, Roi, when it leaves the palace,
follow it.

501
00:38:09,833 --> 00:38:13,125
<i>Keep your distance, some 400 or 500 m.</i>
<i>No need to take risks.</i>

502
00:38:13,208 --> 00:38:14,458
Keila will guide you.

503
00:38:26,750 --> 00:38:29,166
- Yes.
- Damián, you need to come right now.

504
00:38:29,250 --> 00:38:31,416
- Where are you?
<i>- At a party, in a bathroom.</i>

505
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:35,500
{\an8}The duchess brought me here
to offer me a million euros, get this,

506
00:38:35,583 --> 00:38:38,208
<i>to steal her husband's paintings.</i>

507
00:38:38,291 --> 00:38:40,416
- Why?
- Says he no longer has eyes for her.

508
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:41,666
Only for the paintings.

509
00:38:41,750 --> 00:38:43,583
- What madcap idea is that?
<i>- No, wait.</i>

510
00:38:43,666 --> 00:38:45,791
She also says
I'm not leaving until I accept,

511
00:38:45,875 --> 00:38:49,708
and we won't steal <i>Lady with an Ermine</i>
with the police watching us.

512
00:38:49,791 --> 00:38:52,708
She threatened you?
What will you do? Accept?

513
00:38:52,791 --> 00:38:53,791
<i>Of course not!</i>

514
00:38:53,875 --> 00:38:57,791
Because you'll show up with all your magic
and get the idea out of her head.

515
00:38:57,875 --> 00:38:59,375
- What?
<i>- Listen to me.</i>

516
00:38:59,458 --> 00:39:02,166
<i>You'll go to Santa Cruz Square,</i>
<i>to the orange stall,</i>

517
00:39:02,250 --> 00:39:06,416
and tell the two women at the back
that you want Chinese oranges.

518
00:39:06,500 --> 00:39:07,541
You hear me?

519
00:39:09,791 --> 00:39:12,333
What is it? Do you hear me?

520
00:39:13,583 --> 00:39:14,791
Well, well.

521
00:39:14,875 --> 00:39:16,000
Candela.

522
00:39:18,375 --> 00:39:21,166
What a surprise. What are you doing here?

523
00:39:22,416 --> 00:39:23,541
Waiting for me?

524
00:39:24,708 --> 00:39:26,125
Of course I am.

525
00:39:26,833 --> 00:39:29,416
So, I'm here now.

526
00:39:30,166 --> 00:39:34,458
Is there anything else
you don't leave for the end of a date?

527
00:39:35,625 --> 00:39:36,625
One more thing.

528
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:38,125
Want to know what?

529
00:39:52,625 --> 00:39:54,208
Are you still up for it?

530
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:57,500
You great pig.

531
00:39:59,958 --> 00:40:01,666
You think I was born yesterday?

532
00:40:01,750 --> 00:40:04,958
<i>After kissing me in the alley,</i>
<i>which is a commitment,</i>

533
00:40:05,041 --> 00:40:06,750
you got in here with the duchess.

534
00:40:06,833 --> 00:40:09,125
- No.
- With my spittle still in your mouth.

535
00:40:09,208 --> 00:40:11,500
Don't deny it. I saw you with my own eyes.

536
00:40:11,583 --> 00:40:14,958
She beckoned with her finger
as if she were Cleopatra,

537
00:40:15,041 --> 00:40:16,541
and you ran after her.

538
00:40:17,416 --> 00:40:21,625
Fine, the duchess
asked to see me in private, and I agreed,

539
00:40:21,708 --> 00:40:23,083
because I know her husband.

540
00:40:23,166 --> 00:40:26,500
And I intuited
she wanted to discuss something personal.

541
00:40:26,583 --> 00:40:28,208
Important. Tragic, even.

542
00:40:29,166 --> 00:40:31,958
In the end,
she just wanted to talk business.

543
00:40:32,041 --> 00:40:33,250
<i>No, what are you saying?</i>

544
00:40:33,333 --> 00:40:35,750
Business with a lady in a bathroom?

545
00:40:35,833 --> 00:40:37,666
Business? What business?

546
00:40:37,750 --> 00:40:40,583
Backtrack. What business
does one discuss in a bathroom?

547
00:40:40,666 --> 00:40:41,833
Illegal stuff, dammit.

548
00:40:42,416 --> 00:40:43,541
Wouldn't it be leisure?

549
00:40:43,625 --> 00:40:45,208
<i>That's right, leisure.</i>

550
00:40:45,291 --> 00:40:48,791
Take the lesser charge. You're getting
into dicey territory. You'll screw us.

551
00:40:48,875 --> 00:40:49,916
Fine, you're right.

552
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:51,791
The duchess brought me here,

553
00:40:51,875 --> 00:40:55,916
making me believe she wanted
to discuss something urgent, but she

554
00:40:56,833 --> 00:40:57,875
tried to kiss me.

555
00:40:57,958 --> 00:41:00,041
I, of course, said no.

556
00:41:04,583 --> 00:41:06,166
Excuse me, I want…

557
00:41:07,208 --> 00:41:08,958
Chinese oranges.

558
00:41:15,416 --> 00:41:17,541
What? Will you keep lying to my face?

559
00:41:17,625 --> 00:41:19,125
He did nothing.

560
00:41:19,208 --> 00:41:21,000
Are you an altar boy now?

561
00:41:23,833 --> 00:41:26,250
You don't know
who you're talking to, right?

562
00:41:26,333 --> 00:41:27,708
Huh? What is it?

563
00:41:27,791 --> 00:41:29,791
You're not used to a woman like this.

564
00:41:29,875 --> 00:41:31,791
<i>You can't handle her that easily.</i>

565
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:36,708
Since you've followed her movements
and mine with such attention

566
00:41:36,791 --> 00:41:38,958
and you want so badly to suspect me,

567
00:41:39,041 --> 00:41:40,666
I'll tell you something.

568
00:41:40,750 --> 00:41:43,041
We were here no more than three minutes.

569
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:45,458
Enough time to reject a person,

570
00:41:46,041 --> 00:41:49,083
but, you'll have to agree,
not to… satisfy them.

571
00:41:50,958 --> 00:41:52,958
Oh, you silver-tongued devil.

572
00:41:54,041 --> 00:41:55,791
Are you a defense attorney now?

573
00:41:56,791 --> 00:41:57,916
I'll tell you something.

574
00:42:01,083 --> 00:42:04,916
I'll believe you
because no man comes that fast.

575
00:42:05,416 --> 00:42:06,833
And I hope you don't either.

576
00:42:07,541 --> 00:42:11,166
But if you're not going to live up
to that kiss you gave me,

577
00:42:11,916 --> 00:42:15,250
I'd rather you left
and didn't call me again.

578
00:42:43,500 --> 00:42:45,166
I can't believe it.

579
00:42:45,750 --> 00:42:47,833
Are you carrying what I think?

580
00:42:49,250 --> 00:42:52,541
You must be something else
to bring a bag with millions

581
00:42:52,625 --> 00:42:54,250
to a flamenco shindig.

582
00:42:55,041 --> 00:42:56,583
Or I have a festive spirit

583
00:42:56,666 --> 00:42:59,041
and know that the safest place
to keep money

584
00:42:59,125 --> 00:43:00,500
is on oneself.

585
00:43:01,083 --> 00:43:01,916
Play along.

586
00:43:03,083 --> 00:43:05,291
Samuel, we were just wondering

587
00:43:05,375 --> 00:43:08,583
if there wouldn't be
anything more spirituous to drink.

588
00:43:08,666 --> 00:43:10,416
Get us two gin and tonics?

589
00:43:10,500 --> 00:43:13,958
With squeezed lemon
and Madagascar black peppercorns.

590
00:43:17,208 --> 00:43:18,208
Thank you.

591
00:43:22,166 --> 00:43:25,666
It'll take him a while
to find the Madagascar black pepper.

592
00:43:27,833 --> 00:43:29,333
Why exactly are we running?

593
00:43:29,416 --> 00:43:30,916
To lose my babysitter.

594
00:43:31,000 --> 00:43:33,041
I'm confused, and I need clarity.

595
00:43:37,166 --> 00:43:39,791
This way. To the upper floor.

596
00:43:42,375 --> 00:43:44,875
I had an epiphany talking to your partner.

597
00:43:48,083 --> 00:43:49,500
Come this way.

598
00:44:03,875 --> 00:44:05,291
Make yourself comfortable.

599
00:44:30,250 --> 00:44:32,666
Tell me about that epiphany.

600
00:44:33,416 --> 00:44:37,000
I think your partner and my husband

601
00:44:37,083 --> 00:44:39,291
are exactly the same.

602
00:44:40,166 --> 00:44:42,416
The thought crossed my mind, I admit.

603
00:44:42,500 --> 00:44:44,083
And you and I, well…

604
00:44:44,166 --> 00:44:46,250
we take a step back

605
00:44:46,750 --> 00:44:50,166
to let the person we love shine.

606
00:44:50,250 --> 00:44:52,750
That's sexy somehow.

607
00:44:54,583 --> 00:44:56,458
What's sexy about that?

608
00:44:56,958 --> 00:44:58,958
A man sure of himself

609
00:44:59,041 --> 00:45:02,666
doesn't need to be reminded all the time.

610
00:45:04,041 --> 00:45:06,666
He's not constantly trying to surprise

611
00:45:06,750 --> 00:45:11,250
and doesn't go around boasting
about their eccentricities.

612
00:45:13,625 --> 00:45:17,583
We could say
we're like the B-sides of some records,

613
00:45:17,666 --> 00:45:20,708
which are authentic hidden gems.

614
00:45:21,208 --> 00:45:24,500
What do you say to starting a revolution?

615
00:45:24,583 --> 00:45:26,125
You and I.

616
00:45:26,208 --> 00:45:29,375
The revolution of the B-sides.

617
00:45:30,500 --> 00:45:33,250
- Want to betray your husband?
- Until a moment ago, yes.

618
00:45:34,125 --> 00:45:37,291
I wanted to steal his collection

619
00:45:38,333 --> 00:45:39,625
so he'd look at me.

620
00:45:40,958 --> 00:45:42,750
An act of desperation.

621
00:45:43,625 --> 00:45:47,666
But revolution starts with oneself, right?

622
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:51,875
I've always been a faithful wife,

623
00:45:53,208 --> 00:45:54,541
in love.

624
00:45:58,166 --> 00:45:59,833
I won't be that anymore.

625
00:46:02,416 --> 00:46:04,375
Your friend made me think.

626
00:46:04,958 --> 00:46:08,416
Maybe my husband and I
are no longer in love.

627
00:46:11,125 --> 00:46:12,166
And maybe…

628
00:46:14,250 --> 00:46:15,250
Maybe

629
00:46:16,083 --> 00:46:19,833
it's a good time
to start a new chapter in my life.

630
00:46:20,625 --> 00:46:22,250
Shall we get emancipated together?

631
00:46:22,833 --> 00:46:23,916
You and I.

632
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:28,291
We can make a record with two A-sides.

633
00:46:29,541 --> 00:46:31,666
Yours and mine.

634
00:46:37,333 --> 00:46:40,958
Sorry, I'm not much of a music lover, and

635
00:46:41,458 --> 00:46:43,541
I'm not sure I understand you.

636
00:46:44,458 --> 00:46:48,541
When I was looking at the Macarena,

637
00:46:50,166 --> 00:46:54,750
I asked her to please help me figure out
what to do with my life.

638
00:46:58,958 --> 00:47:00,208
And you appeared.

639
00:47:00,708 --> 00:47:03,333
You, with your grace,

640
00:47:04,208 --> 00:47:05,791
your poise…

641
00:47:06,666 --> 00:47:09,541
That elegant bag full of millions.

642
00:47:11,750 --> 00:47:15,208
Don't you think that's a strong signal?

643
00:47:16,541 --> 00:47:19,416
I really think
you're the perfect other half

644
00:47:19,500 --> 00:47:21,375
to start my revolution…

645
00:47:23,250 --> 00:47:25,291
and make my debut as an unfaithful wife.

646
00:47:28,708 --> 00:47:29,666
What do you say?

647
00:47:45,541 --> 00:47:47,166
I think your watch is vibrating.

648
00:47:50,875 --> 00:47:52,791
It's a call.

649
00:47:53,291 --> 00:47:54,375
Excuse me.

650
00:48:02,250 --> 00:48:03,791
"Put in your earpiece."

651
00:48:13,583 --> 00:48:14,458
Yes, Keila.

652
00:48:14,541 --> 00:48:16,458
The money's moved, but inside the palace.

653
00:48:16,541 --> 00:48:19,250
Maybe the duke
is packing the bundles again

654
00:48:19,333 --> 00:48:20,958
or bagging them.

655
00:48:21,041 --> 00:48:23,375
I don't think so. It's underground.

656
00:48:23,458 --> 00:48:26,416
I lost the signal
26 meters under the palace,

657
00:48:26,500 --> 00:48:30,125
below what the blueprints
show as the chapel.

658
00:48:30,208 --> 00:48:33,083
But the plans
show nothing under that chapel.

659
00:48:33,791 --> 00:48:34,916
Unless…

660
00:48:35,916 --> 00:48:38,708
He has a vault under his palace.

661
00:48:38,791 --> 00:48:41,166
And that's why you lost the GPS signal.

662
00:48:42,291 --> 00:48:43,708
- Roi.
- Still in position.

663
00:48:43,791 --> 00:48:47,208
Go with Keila and scour the registries
for any info on that chapel.

664
00:48:50,291 --> 00:48:51,541
Bruce, you too.

665
00:48:51,625 --> 00:48:52,958
Copy. Going to the boat.

666
00:49:02,833 --> 00:49:03,791
Hello.

667
00:49:04,541 --> 00:49:05,541
<i>Hi.</i>

668
00:49:06,291 --> 00:49:08,541
- Hi.
<i>- I have a surprise for you.</i>

669
00:49:08,625 --> 00:49:09,750
<i>I'm in Seville.</i>

670
00:49:09,833 --> 00:49:11,291
I'm looking at your boat.

671
00:49:29,750 --> 00:49:30,750
<i>Hello?</i>

672
00:49:33,208 --> 00:49:35,583
Good afternoon, everyone.

673
00:49:35,666 --> 00:49:40,041
I met this goddess only a few hours ago,

674
00:49:40,541 --> 00:49:42,666
but I've already experienced more emotions

675
00:49:42,750 --> 00:49:45,708
than many married couples
by their 50th anniversary.

676
00:49:45,791 --> 00:49:52,041
I could be dead, burned, imprisoned,
and practically divorced, but

677
00:49:52,708 --> 00:49:54,291
she gave me a chance.

678
00:49:54,791 --> 00:49:58,541
And to celebrate it,
I've asked her to sing this song.

679
00:49:59,041 --> 00:50:00,375
Give her a big hand.

680
00:50:07,125 --> 00:50:08,375
Come on!

681
00:50:12,083 --> 00:50:13,000
That's it!

682
00:50:29,083 --> 00:50:30,083
Olé!

683
00:50:54,125 --> 00:50:55,125
Hey.

684
00:51:13,208 --> 00:51:15,333
We have the coordinates
to Ali Baba's cave.

685
00:51:15,416 --> 00:51:17,625
Very well. Where is that lair?

686
00:51:18,625 --> 00:51:21,166
At the duke's palace. Under the chapel.

687
00:51:21,250 --> 00:51:22,625
He must have a vault.

688
00:51:22,708 --> 00:51:25,625
We lost the signal
at the depth of a fourth floor.

689
00:51:27,416 --> 00:51:31,500
So we have located our loot.
Now we only need to go and grab it.

690
00:51:31,583 --> 00:51:32,666
How wonderful.

691
00:51:45,041 --> 00:51:46,625
I love this place.

692
00:51:46,708 --> 00:51:47,791
And the duchess?

693
00:51:47,875 --> 00:51:50,083
Did you talk her out of that absurd idea?

694
00:51:50,166 --> 00:51:51,583
- That one, yes.
- Good.

695
00:51:51,666 --> 00:51:55,208
Now she wants to betray him
with an affair. Says I'm her other half.

696
00:51:55,291 --> 00:51:58,250
It's the third time I've seen her,
and she's saying the Macarena

697
00:51:58,333 --> 00:52:00,000
signaled I was to be her lover.

698
00:52:00,083 --> 00:52:02,916
She leaned in to whisper,
and I had to roll my sleeves down

699
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:04,916
to hide my hair standing on end.

700
00:52:05,000 --> 00:52:08,916
She wants to make a record of A-sides
with me. I don't know what to say.

701
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:12,375
The lady unsettles you.
Don't worry. That's all good news.

702
00:52:12,458 --> 00:52:14,416
Keep her eating out of your hand.

703
00:52:14,500 --> 00:52:15,416
What are you saying?

704
00:52:15,500 --> 00:52:17,541
The better half, pulling the strings.

705
00:52:17,625 --> 00:52:20,333
Get close. Grow distant.

706
00:52:20,416 --> 00:52:23,833
It's your turn to become
a Latin lover, Damián. A predator.

707
00:52:29,500 --> 00:52:30,583
How are you?

708
00:52:31,791 --> 00:52:33,208
With Madagascar pepper.

709
00:52:33,791 --> 00:52:35,833
I heard you were working on my commission.

710
00:52:35,916 --> 00:52:39,333
That's right. I came
because I must ask you for something.

711
00:52:40,291 --> 00:52:43,250
We can't continue working
on our plan on the boat.

712
00:52:43,333 --> 00:52:45,166
So many boards and sensitive material.

713
00:52:45,250 --> 00:52:46,833
It can be seen from the outside.

714
00:52:47,333 --> 00:52:49,416
We'll need a more discreet space.

715
00:52:49,500 --> 00:52:53,583
We thought maybe
your palace's north wing, the tower.

716
00:52:53,666 --> 00:52:54,958
How is everybody?

717
00:52:59,625 --> 00:53:01,333
- Hi.
- Hi, darling.

718
00:53:02,416 --> 00:53:06,250
You know? I decided Simón and his friends

719
00:53:06,333 --> 00:53:08,750
will be our guests at the palace
for a few days.

720
00:53:08,833 --> 00:53:10,000
What do you think?

721
00:53:11,125 --> 00:53:13,708
A very stimulating idea.

722
00:53:18,500 --> 00:53:20,791
I'll have to keep you
on a short leash, huh?

723
00:53:21,916 --> 00:53:23,875
This man just loves to make an escape.

724
00:53:24,958 --> 00:53:28,625
Excuse me, but we're having an affair.
Baby boo.

725
00:53:28,708 --> 00:53:30,250
Well, this…

726
00:53:30,750 --> 00:53:32,083
This is Candela.

727
00:53:32,166 --> 00:53:33,500
Happy birthday.

728
00:53:34,083 --> 00:53:35,250
Thank you.

729
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:39,875
By the way, Candela,
this is Damián, my partner.

730
00:53:40,375 --> 00:53:43,666
We were discussing some business
with the duke and duchess.

731
00:53:43,750 --> 00:53:48,041
Another? Or the same one you discussed
in the Niña de los Peines bathroom?

732
00:53:48,125 --> 00:53:50,833
No, another one, Candela.

733
00:53:50,916 --> 00:53:52,208
Well…

734
00:53:52,291 --> 00:53:55,250
Don't you and your friend
like your money, huh?

735
00:54:01,708 --> 00:54:02,916
Will you excuse me?

736
00:54:04,500 --> 00:54:05,833
Did I say something wrong?

737
00:54:05,916 --> 00:54:07,208
No.

738
00:54:23,875 --> 00:54:25,708
Have you seen the bag that was here?

739
00:54:26,291 --> 00:54:28,916
What was in that bag? You look worried.

740
00:57:06,333 --> 00:57:08,250
Subtitle translation by:
Soledad Etchemendy

